  <p><a href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5123456&amp;utm_source=alert">Statistical Factors and the Winner&#39;s Curse in Anomaly Selection</a></p>
  <p>Jane Q. Researcher, John Smith and Wei Zhang</p>
  <p>Researchers select the best-performing anomalies from hundreds of candidates and then report their in-sample Sharpe ratios. We show that this selection step inflates reported performance by an amount that depends on the factor structure of returns, and we propose a bootstrap correction that remains valid when the top candidates are nearly tied.</p>
