<tr><td>
  <p><a href="https://ssrn.com/abstract=5198765">Learning Policies Under Imperfect Implementation by AI Agents</a></p>
  <p>Ana Lopez</p>
  <p>Automated agents increasingly execute business decisions, but their execution is noisy: they sometimes fail to follow the policy they were given. We model noncompliance explicitly and derive estimators for the value of the intended policy that remain consistent under imperfect execution.</p>
